[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":29},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-7,"_20":21,"_22":-7,"_23":-7,"_24":25},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":26,"_13":26,"_27":28},"id","guimond-iniciante","nome","Guimond with 2 algorithms","rascunho",false,"html","<p>Full <a href=\"/en/glossary#guimond\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it twists the corners so white and yellow are on top and bottom (mixed), separates the two colors and finishes with Ortega's…\">Guimond</a> has 22 algorithms (16 for orientation and 6 for separation), plus <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a>. To learn it, you can follow the same path with 2: <strong><code>R&#39; F U&#39; R</code></strong> to orient and the <strong>A-perm</strong> to permute, plus a 3-turn trick for separation. It&#39;s slower, but the steps are the same: orient, separate and permute.</p>\n<p>Start with <a href=\"/en/2x2/guimond/tres-quartos\">¾ of a face</a>: with 3 bottom corners already right, orientation takes fewer repetitions.</p>\n<h2>1. Orientation with R&#39; F U&#39; R</h2>\n<p>The algorithm twists two corners at once: the top one, at <strong>front-right</strong>, with white or yellow facing right; and the bottom one, at <strong>back-right</strong>, with its color facing back. The other corners may move around, but the right ones stay right.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R' U F' R&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;R' F U' R&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;wy&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"R' F U' R\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/58d5196fe1ad7a27-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/58d5196fe1ad7a27-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/58d5196fe1ad7a27-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/58d5196fe1ad7a27-3.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/58d5196fe1ad7a27-4.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The twisted top corner at front-right, with its color facing right (the bottom one, at the back, isn&#39;t visible). After the algorithm, both are right.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<ol>\n<li>Turn <code>D</code> until a twisted bottom corner is at back-right. If you can choose, one with its color facing back.</li>\n<li>Turn <code>U</code> until a twisted top corner is at front-right. If you can choose, one with its color facing right.</li>\n<li>If the top one points to the front and the bottom one to the right, turn the cube over (<code>x2</code>): the two swap places and end up the way the algorithm needs.</li>\n<li>Do <code>R&#39; F U&#39; R</code> and look again. Repeat until the top and bottom faces have only white and yellow.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If all the twisted corners are in one layer, take one to the other: keep them on top (<code>x2</code>, if needed), turn <code>U</code> until one is at front-right (preferably with the back-right one already right) and do <code>R2</code>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> sometimes the algorithm just moves the twisted corner somewhere else. Keep going: with the choices above, orientation always finishes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>2. Separation with R2 U R2</h2>\n<p>The trick moves only two corners to the other layer: the top one at <strong>back-left</strong> and the bottom one at <strong>back-right</strong>. The others stay in their layer.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2 U' R2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;R2 U R2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;wy&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"R2 U R2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/584357222a504fbe-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/584357222a504fbe-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/584357222a504fbe-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/584357222a504fbe-3.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>One white on top and one yellow on the bottom: <code>R2 U R2</code> swaps them.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<ol>\n<li>If there are 3 or 4 whites on top, turn the cube over (<code>x2</code>).</li>\n<li>Turn <code>U</code> until a top white is at back-left, and <code>D</code> until a bottom yellow is at back-right.</li>\n<li>Do <code>R2 U R2</code>. Repeat until all the yellow is on top (twice at most).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>3. Permutation with the A-perm</h2>\n<p class=\"formula\"><code>R' F R' B2 R F' R' B2 R2</code></p>\n<p>Look at the sides of the top layer. A side with both colors matching is a <strong>bar</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>4 bars:</strong> the layer is done.</li>\n<li><strong>1 bar:</strong> turn <code>U</code> until it is at the back and do the A-perm.</li>\n<li><strong>None:</strong> do the A-perm from any side. A bar shows up: take it to the back and do it again.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2 B2 R F R' B2 R F' R&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/e045eded7f4dbd7f.svg\" alt=\"One bar, at the back: the A-perm finishes the layer.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>One bar, at the back: the A-perm finishes the layer.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F R U' R' U' R U R' F' R U R' U' R' F R F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/d22ea6df6058cb7d.svg\" alt=\"No bars: the A-perm makes one appear.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>No bars: the A-perm makes one appear.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>Then turn the cube over (<code>x2</code>) and do the same with the other layer. At the end, turn <code>U</code> or <code>D</code> until the sides match: the cube is solved.</p>\n<p>When you&#39;re comfortable, swap each step for the full Guimond algorithms: <a href=\"/en/2x2/guimond/orientacao\">orientation</a>, <a href=\"/en/2x2/guimond/separacao\">separation</a> and <a href=\"/en/2x2/ortega-pbl\">PBL</a>.</p>\n","treino","metodos",[],"anterior","proximo","grupos",[],"2x2","endereco","/2x2/",{"_30":31,"_32":33},"cubos",[36,37,38,39,40,41,42],"idiomas",[34,35],"pt","en",{"_11":51,"_13":51},{"_11":26,"_13":26},{"_11":50,"_13":50},{"_11":49,"_13":49},{"_11":47,"_13":48},{"_11":45,"_13":46},{"_11":43,"_13":44},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
